Patches applied to the pristine ntfs-3g_ntfsprogs-2026.9.28 tarball by
../unpack.sh.

They apply with `patch -p1` from inside src/, in filename order.  Each one
starts with a few lines of prose saying what it does and why, then the diff.

  0001-old-permission-bit-names.patch
        S_IREAD, S_IWRITE and S_IEXEC are defined from the POSIX names
        where the libc lacks them.

  0002-operands-after-options.patch
        mkntfs, ntfsfix and ntfsinfo find their device when getopt() stops
        at the first operand (POSIX) instead of returning operands in
        order.

